<main id="main"><section class="pageHero compact"><div class="container"><span class="kicker">Trust & safety</span><h1>Abuse Reporting</h1><p>Report activity that appears to violate law or our Acceptable Use Policy.</p></div></section><section class="section"><div class="container legalProse"><h2>How to report abuse</h2><p>Email <a href="mailto:<%= site.emails.abuse %>"><%= site.emails.abuse %></a>. Please include the relevant IP address or hostname, timestamps with timezone, a concise description of the issue, and supporting logs, URLs or headers where available.</p><h2>What happens next</h2><p>We review credible reports and may request more information. Appropriate action can include contacting the customer, restricting traffic, isolating a service, preserving relevant records, suspending access or escalating to an upstream provider or competent authority where necessary.</p><h2>Good-faith reporting</h2><p>Please do not attempt to gain unauthorised access, exploit systems or collect unnecessary personal data while investigating a report. Security researchers should minimise impact and provide enough information for us to reproduce or assess the issue safely.</p></div></section></main>
